            <ArticleTitle>De novo design and synthesis of a μ-conotoxin KIIIA peptidomimetic.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4892-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.06.086</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)00819-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>μ-Conotoxin KIIIA blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and displays potent analgesic activity in mice models for pain. Structure-activity studies with KIIIA have shown that residues important for sodium channel activity are presented on an α-helix. Herein, we report the de novo design and synthesis of a three-residue (Lys7, Trp8, His12) peptidomimetic based on a novel diketopiperazine (DKP) carboxamide scaffold.</AbstractText>
